this is a collection of bugs that i consider definite bugs, except
that they might be features.  in other words, you could argue that
they're deliberate design decisions.  some of these bug description
might be considered SPOILERs.

i'm sorry, but i don't know whether any of these have been mentioned before or
not (since i haven't been very good about reading rec.games.nethack).

this is nethack 3.0 patch level 7, on a 386 PC running AT&T SVR3.2


			*** MILD SPOILER ***

1) "I choked over my food while eating a corpse without ever being
	warned.  the food was an orange dragon corpse and i was satiated
	when i started; however it had been awhile since i'd eaten."
	looking at the code in "lesshungry", it appears that if the
	nutritional content of the food is high enough, i can run
	u.uhunger over 2000 before i ever get warned (say if the 
	nutrution per turn is >= 500; another way would have been
	to continue eating after the choke message at a previous time
	so that u.uhunger was already >= 1500.  i don't think i had
	continued eating after such a message recently, but a 
	continued string of "Stop eating?" "n" could push you over
	the edge i think.

	I can recreate this by starting the game, wishing for and eating
	an orange dragon corpse, getting "You're having a hard time getting
	all of it down.", wishing for another, and then getting
	"you choke".

    could somebody please post a reasonable description of how choking
	is supposed to work?  the behavior is not clear from a short glance
	through the code.  it appears the intention is to always ask 
	"Stop eating" before choking ensues, but that's not the behavior.

    or perhaps you are guaranteed not to choke if you never start eating
	from the "satiated" state.  i guess i don't like that much.  i've
	never choked if i started eating from a non-satiated state, though
	i haven't been paying much attention.

2) I've made a small hack to the wizard code so that a wizard can
	monkey with any random character, and then save it back
	so the person can use it as a normal player again (or
	recreate a character from a bones file (with some effort--but
	the previous level maps are, of course, lost)).

    Does anybody want a copy of this hack?

			*** SPOILER ***

3) You burn food faster when your hungry!  At 1.5 the rate of
	normal consumption.  Is this a bug? Logically (yes, i know
	logic doesn't apply) your metabolism should slow down
	when you're hungry.  (see the code near front of 
	gethungry() in eat.c).

4) SIGSEGV and SIGBUS dumps don't cause a game to be saved, while
	SIGHUP does.  why not?  is this some sort of weird anti-cheating
	thing (preventing you from taking advantage of bugs that cause
	SIGSEGV or SIGBUS)?  it seems to cause more harm than good.
	
    here's the contextual diff for my fix (feed it to patch on 
	src/unixmain.c):

*** /tmp/,RCSt1a08352	Mon May  7 23:57:35 1990
